=head2 get_context

  my $context = $client->calls($call_sid)->siprec->get_context($sid);

Returns a C<SiprecContext>, and makes no request.


=head1 SiprecContext

Returned by C<< $client->calls($call_sid)->siprec($sid) >>. It makes no request
until one of these methods is called.

=head2 update

  my $siprec = $client->calls($call_sid)->siprec($sid)->update($status);

Stop a Siprec using either the SID of the Siprec resource or the C<name> used
when creating the resource. Returns a C<SiprecInstance>.

The required values are:

=over

=item C<$status>

Must be C<stopped>.

=back

=head1 SiprecInstance

See also L<Twilio::InstanceResource>.

It has C<update>, which work as they do on the context.

Its fields are:

=over

=item account_sid

The SID of the L<Account|https://www.twilio.com/docs/iam/api/account> that
created this Siprec resource.

=item call_sid

The SID of the L<Call|https://www.twilio.com/docs/voice/api/call-resource> the
Siprec resource is associated with.

=item date_updated

The date and time in GMT that this resource was last updated, specified in
L<RFC 2822|https://www.ietf.org/rfc/rfc2822.txt> format. A L<Time::Piece>
object in UTC. See L<Twilio::Deserialize/date_time>.

=item name

The user-specified name of this Siprec, if one was given when the Siprec was
created. This may be used to stop the Siprec.

=item sid

The SID of the Siprec resource.

=item status

One of C<in-progress> or C<stopped>.

=item uri

The URI of the resource, relative to C<https://api.twilio.com>.

=back

